eau is not an added premise of the full-support theorem. The boundary-layer estimate itself does not use minimality. It uses the finite plateau and terminal cusp, not a derivative estimate uniform up to time 1. Constants depend on the fixed coefficient/plateau; no quantitative bound uniform over minimizers is claimed.","citation_ids":["support_terminal_source","support_terminal_defect_lean_source"],"evidence_ids":["support_source_bindings_20261024","support_graph_semantic_review_pending"],"id":"support.terminal_defect","kind":"claim","label":"Square-root terminal deficit on a finite plateau","locator":"variation.tex:144–207; eq:terminal-layer; ContactPotential.lean:124–208","source_id":"support_tex_variation","statement":"For gamma in U with gamma=c on (a,1), where 0<=a<1 and finite c>=0, and its controlled diffusion, there are C>0 and t0<1 such that 1-q(t)>=C*sqrt(1-t) for t0<t<1. The tilted heat kernel (ordinary heat kernel for c=0) supplies a uniform positive density bound near x=0 at late times; both terminal signs retain positive tilted probability on |x|<=sqrt(1-t).","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.terminal_defect","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.no_terminal_gap","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.no_terminal_gap%22%2C%22support.terminal_defect%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22support.no_terminal_gap%22%2C%22support.terminal_defect%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.terminal_defect"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286